## Quick Installation

### 1. Download Complete System

Save all the scripts from the previous artifacts to your system, then run:

```bash
# Make all scripts executable
chmod +x *.sh

# Run the complete installation
sudo bash install-login-monitoring.sh
```

### 2. Configure Your Settings

```bash
# Edit main configuration
sudo nano /etc/fail2ban/nftban.conf
```

**Key settings to configure:**
```bash
# Your email for alerts
NFTBAN_F2B_RECIPIENT="your-email@domain.com"

# Enable specific monitoring
NFTBAN_F2B_ROOT_LOGIN_ALERT="true"    # CRITICAL: Root login alerts
NFTBAN_F2B_SUDO_ALERT="true"          # Sudo command monitoring  
NFTBAN_F2B_SSH_LOGIN_ALERT="false"    # All SSH logins (can be noisy)
NFTBAN_F2B_FAILED_LOGIN_THRESHOLD="5" # Alert after N failed attempts
```

### 3. Start Monitoring

```bash
# Generate fail2ban configurations
sudo fail2ban-template-generator.sh --reload

# Start login monitoring
sudo systemctl start nftban-advanced-login-monitor

# Check status
sudo systemctl status nftban-advanced-login-monitor
```

