## Detailed Installation Steps

### Step 1: System Preparation

```bash
# Update system
sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y  # Debian/Ubuntu
# sudo yum update -y                    # RHEL/CentOS
# sudo dnf update -y                    # Fedora

# Install basic dependencies
sudo apt install -y fail2ban nftables rsyslog git
```

### Step 2: Create Directory Structure

```bash
# Create required directories
sudo mkdir -p /etc/fail2ban/{jail-templates.d,jail.d/backups,action.d,filter.d}
sudo mkdir -p /usr/local/bin
sudo mkdir -p /var/log
```

### Step 3: Install Scripts

Copy each script from the artifacts to the appropriate location:

```bash
# Main template generator (from first artifact)
sudo cp fail2ban-template-generator.sh /usr/local/bin/
sudo chmod +x /usr/local/bin/fail2ban-template-generator.sh

# Email system setup (from second artifact)  
sudo cp email-system-setup.sh /usr/local/bin/
sudo chmod +x /usr/local/bin/email-system-setup.sh

# Advanced login monitor (from second artifact)
sudo cp advanced-login-monitor.sh /usr/local/bin/
sudo chmod +x /usr/local/bin/advanced-login-monitor.sh

# Installation script (from second artifact)
sudo cp install-login-monitoring.sh /usr/local/bin/
sudo chmod +x /usr/local/bin/install-login-monitoring.sh
```

### Step 4: Configure Email System

```bash
# Detect current email system
sudo email-system-setup.sh detect

# Install if none found
sudo email-system-setup.sh install

# Test email functionality
sudo email-system-setup.sh test root
```

### Step 5: Configure NFTBAN

```bash
# Create/edit configuration file
sudo nano /etc/fail2ban/nftban.conf
```

**Example production configuration:**
```bash
# Email Settings
NFTBAN_F2B_RECIPIENT="security@company.com"
NFTBAN_F2B_SENDER="nftban@$(hostname -f)"

# Security Settings  
NFTBAN_F2B_DEF_BAN_TIME="3600"           # 1 hour
NFTBAN_F2B_MAXRETRY="3"                  # Stricter for production
NFTBAN_F2B_FINDTIME="600"                # 10 minutes

# Login Monitoring
NFTBAN_F2B_LOGIN_MONITOR="true"
NFTBAN_F2B_ROOT_LOGIN_ALERT="true"       # CRITICAL alerts
NFTBAN_F2B_SUDO_ALERT="true"             # Monitor sudo usage
NFTBAN_F2B_SSH_LOGIN_ALERT="false"       # Only suspicious logins
NFTBAN_F2B_FAILED_LOGIN_THRESHOLD="3"    # Alert after 3 failures

# Enhanced Features
NFTBAN_F2B_GEOIP_ENABLE="true"          # Include location data
NFTBAN_F2B_WHOIS_ENABLE="true"          # Include network info
NFTBAN_F2B_AGGRESSIVE_MODE="false"       # Standard security

# Ignore internal networks
NFTBAN_F2B_IGNOREIP="127.0.0.1/8 ::1 10.0.0.0/8 192.168.0.0/16"
```

