## Configuration Reference

### Alert Types and Priorities

| Alert Type | Trigger | Priority | Description |
|------------|---------|----------|-------------|
| `CRITICAL` | Root login | Urgent | Any root access via SSH/console/su |
| `ATTACK` | Multiple failed logins | High | Exceeds threshold from single IP |
| `HIGH_RISK_SUDO` | Dangerous commands | High | Commands affecting system security |
| `LOGIN` | SSH successful login | Normal | Regular user SSH access |
| `SUDO` | Standard sudo usage | Normal | Regular privileged commands |

### Risk Assessment Levels

**CRITICAL Commands:**
- `rm -rf`, `dd`, `mkfs`, `fdisk` - Data destruction
- `shred`, `wipe` - Secure deletion

**HIGH Risk Commands:**  
- `chmod`, `chown`, `usermod`, `userdel` - Permission changes
- `passwd`, `visudo`, `crontab -e` - Security configuration

**MEDIUM Risk Commands:**
- `systemctl`, `service` - Service management  
- `mount`, `umount` - Filesystem operations
- `iptables`, `ufw` - Firewall changes

### Email System Compatibility

| System | Status | Auto-Install | Notes |
|--------|--------|--------------|-------|
| **Postfix** | ✅ Full Support | Yes | Recommended, local delivery |
| **Exim4** | ✅ Full Support | No | Common on Debian |
| **Sendmail** | ✅ Compatible | No | Traditional Unix MTA |
| **MSMTP** | ✅ Compatible | No | Lightweight SMTP client |
| **SSMTP** | ✅ Compatible | No | Simple SMTP forwarder |

